-- Migration 27: verify verdict fields on `source_section`.
-- verify_clean_section used to record its verdict as a `verify_flag`
-- source_insight. That was the wrong table: Notebook.get_context() injects every
-- insight into the LLM prompt verbatim and uncapped, so ~114K chars of vision-model
-- proofreading notes rode into every chat turn on a 472-section textbook, and
-- create_insight_command embedded each one into vector search. Diagnostics about
-- how well we read the book are not knowledge about the book.
-- The verdict now lives on the section it describes: queryable ("which chapters
-- are still on the raw parse?"), badgeable in the reader, and invisible to the
-- LLM -- get_outline() selects an explicit column list, so new fields here are
-- structurally unable to leak back into context.
-- `option<string>` is mandatory on both: source_section is SCHEMAFULL and every
-- pre-existing row has neither field, so a non-optional TYPE would make every
-- later UPDATE of those rows fail schema validation (see migration 26).
-- verify_status is one of 'clean' | 'rejected' | 'skipped'; NONE means verify
-- never reached this section.
-- Comments live on full lines ONLY (the runner strips whole-line -- comments but
-- flattens everything else to one line).

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS verify_status ON TABLE source_section TYPE option<string>;

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS verify_reason ON TABLE source_section TYPE option<string>;

UPDATE source_section SET verify_status = 'clean' WHERE verify_status = NONE AND cleaned_content != NONE AND cleaned_content != '';
